чЙ‰чЙ‰чЙ \"I don't normally feel moved to review books, but this one blew me away! I was gripped from begining to end.\"‰чЙ‰чЙ‰чЙ‰чЙ‰чЙ \"I felt like I was running right alongside her.\"BOOK DESCRIPTION\"When I ran, I ran for pleasure. I didn‰ЫЄt run for times, to win, to impress: I ran for me. When I ran my bum cheeks rubbed together, so much so that if I was going on a long run I‰ЫЄd have to ‰Ычlube up‰ЫЄ. I maintained that I was not a ‰Ычreal‰ЫЄ runner ‰ЫТ I just liked to run so that I could eat cake.\"Anna was never anything like those ‰Ычreal‰ЫЄ runners on telly ‰ЫТ all spindly limbs, tiny shorts and split times ‰ЫТ but when she read about New Zealand‰ЫЄs 3,000-kilometre-long Te Araroa Trail, she began to wonder‰Ы? perhaps being a ‰Ычreal‰ЫЄ runner was overrated.Maybe she could just run it anyway?Travelling alone through New Zealand‰ЫЄs backcountry for 148 days, she scrambled through forests, along ridge-lines, over mountain passes, along beaches and across swollen rivers. Running up to 52 kilometres in a day, she slept wild most nights, and was taken into the homes and hearts of the kiwi people in between.The Pants of Perspective is a witty, colourful and at times painfully raw account of a journey to the edge of what a woman believes herself to be capable of. It is a coming-of-age story which will lead you on a roller coaster ride through fear, vulnerability courage and failure. For anyone who has ever dreamt of taking on a great challenge, but felt too afraid to begin ‰ЫТ this story is for you.‰Єґ The books in the 'Anna's Adventures' series can be read in any order ‰Єґ\u003cbr\u003e\nDimensions: 127 x 203\u003cbr\u003e\nAuthor: Anna McNuff\u003cbr\u003e\nISBN: 9781999765804\u003cbr\u003e\nFormat: Paperback\u003cbr\u003e\nPages: 438\u003c\/p\u003e","brand":"bookhero.ae","offers":[{"title":"Default Title","offer_id":45199367700633,"sku":"9RE9781999765804","price":10.0,"currency_code":"AED","in_stock":true}],"thumbnail_url":"\/\/cdn.shopify.com\/s\/files\/1\/0580\/5696\/6297\/files\/67c9c1671ab56_The_20Pants_20Of_20Perspective-_20One_20woman_s_203_000_20kilometre_20running_20adventure_20through_20the_20wilds_20of_20New_20Zealand_20Anna_20McNuff.jpg?v=1741352588"},{"product_id":"the-ruby-airship-the-diamond-thief","title":"The Ruby Airship (The Diamond Thief)","description":"\u003cp\u003eTrapeze-artist RÌ©my has left the circus and her life as a thief, but she doubts that detective Thaddeus Rec will ever truly trust her. Feeling torn between her new life and her old, RÌ©my decides to return to France and her old circus with Yannick, an old friend who unexpectedly appears.Meanwhile, Thaddeus is sure that Yannick is up to no good. He's determined to find them and win RÌ©my back, even if he must risk a journey by airship to do so.\u003cbr\u003e\nDimensions: 129 x 198\u003cbr\u003e\nAuthor: Sharon Gosling\u003cbr\u003e\nISBN: 9781782020721\u003cbr\u003e\nFormat: Paperback\u003cbr\u003e\nPages: 349\u003c\/p\u003e","brand":"bookhero.ae","offers":[{"title":"Default Title","offer_id":45232841392281,"sku":"16RA19781782020721","price":20.0,"currency_code":"AED","in_stock":true}],"thumbnail_url":"\/\/cdn.shopify.com\/s\/files\/1\/0580\/5696\/6297\/files\/67dc21a176a21_The_20Ruby_20Airship_20_The_20Diamond_20Thief_20Sharon_20Gosling.jpg?v=1752084544"},{"product_id":"scarecrow-and-the-army-of-thieves","title":"Scarecrow and the Army of Thieves","description":"\u003cp\u003eAt an abandoned Soviet base in the Arctic, a battle to save all life on Earth is about to begin?THE SECRET BASEIt is a top-secret base known only as Dragon Island. A long-forgotten relic of the Cold War, it houses a weapon of terrible destructive force, a weapon that has just been re-activated.AN ARMY OF MURDERERSWhen Dragon Island is seized by a brutal terrorist force calling itself the Army of Thieves, the fate of the world suddenly hangs in the balance. But there are no crack units close enough to get to Dragon in time to stop the Army setting off the weapon. ONE SMALL TEAMExcept, that is, for a small equipment-testing team up in the Arctic led by a Marine captain named Schofield, call-sign SCARECROW. It's not a strike team; just a handful of Marines and civilians. It's not equipped to attack a fortified island held by a small army. But it will go in anyway, because someone has to.THE ULTIMATE HERO IS BACK, FACING THE ULTIMATE ARMY OF VILLAINS.\u003cbr\u003e\nDimensions: 146 x 218\u003cbr\u003e\nAuthor: Matthew Reilly\u003cbr\u003e\nISBN: 9781409110972\u003cbr\u003e\nFormat: Hardcover\u003cbr\u003e\nPages: 416\u003c\/p\u003e","brand":"bookhero.ae","offers":[{"title":"Default Title","offer_id":45233041375385,"sku":"11RF9781409110972","price":20.0,"currency_code":"AED","in_stock":true}],"thumbnail_url":"\/\/cdn.shopify.com\/s\/files\/1\/0580\/5696\/6297\/files\/67dc1ece186ec_Scarecrow_20and_20the_20Army_20of_20Thieves_20Matthew_20Reilly.jpg?v=1742490129"},{"product_id":"the-five-greatest-warriors-jack-west-series","title":"The Five Greatest Warriors (Jack West Series)","description":"\u003cp\u003eThe end is approaching ... Can Jack West unravel the ancient secrets of the Five Greatest Warriors and save the world?With the end of the world fast approaching, Jack West Jnr must rebuild the final pieces of the fabled, ancient 'Machine' - the only thing that can prevent global catastrophe. But he is out of clues, out of leads ... until he is presented with an ancient text about five unnamed warriors, great historical figures who were all in some way connected to the mysterious Machine. And so Jack and his loyal team set out to discover their identities - and their secrets.Soon Jack is on the trail of a legendary list of greats: from Moses to Genghis Khan and Napoleon, and finally to one most unlikely warrior, the unknown 'Fifth', who, it is said, will be there 'at the end of all things...'\u003cbr\u003e\nDimensions: 143 x 220\u003cbr\u003e\nAuthor: Matthew Reilly\u003cbr\u003e\nISBN: 9781409112662\u003cbr\u003e\nFormat: Hardcover\u00